    "content": "Wake Forest University is a highly selective private liberal arts university in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, known for its small class sizes (11:1 student-faculty ratio) and commitment to \"Pro Humanitate\". It offers top-ranked programs in business, accounting, and liberal arts, with a 21.67% acceptance rate (2024) and tuition of $64,758 (2023-24). Admissions and Rankings Acceptance Rate: Approximately 22% (2024). Admissions Data: Highly competitive with ACT scores ranging from 32-34 and high schoolers often ranking top in their class. The school is test-optional. Rankings: Ranked #51 in National Universities and #12 in Best Undergraduate Teaching by U.S. News & World Report. Undergraduate Enrollment: ~5,400–5,500 students. Academic and Student Life Academics: Known for strong programs in business (finance, management) and communication. Campus Life: Known as \"Demon Deacons,\" the school competes in the Atlantic Coast Conference (ACC). Location: Winston-Salem, NC, with a 340-acre campus and additional facilities at Wake Downtown in the Innovation Quarter. Experience: Over 72% of undergraduates participate in study abroad programs. Notable Aspects Tuition: $64,758 for the 2023-2024 academic year. Notable Alumni: Chris Paul (NBA player), Tim Duncan (NBA player), David Alan Grier (actor/comedian). Campus Dining: The \"Pit\" is the main dining hall. Note: The town of Wake Forest, NC, is a separate entity located near Raleigh, often confused with the university located in Winston-Salem.",
